--- MODEL OUTPUT ---
The void ripples. Three cards rise from nowhere and hang before you, edges glowing like frost-rimmed steel.

First turns The High Priestess, moon-white and still. Her pillars bracket a face you almost recognize. A hush slides through your ribs, as if someone just whispered your true name.

Second flips: Six of Cups. Two children trade a wooden cup on a summer porch you swear you’ve smelled before. Warm sugar drifts across your tongue.

Third: Knight of Wands. A rider in cracked leather jerkin spurs a chestnut mare across dry scrubland. Dust stings your shins; you feel the horse’s pulse knock against your own calves.

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.

The void thins to dawn. Cobblestones print themselves under your boots, and the scent of baking rye slips down the alley ahead.

