--- MODEL OUTPUT ---
You wake in a narrow attic room at the Broken Lantern Inn, Elaris Hollow. A blade of morning light slips through the warped shutter and lands across your eyes. The straw mattress rustles as you sit up; woodsmoke and last night’s ale cling to the blanket.

Your fingers brush the clay cup on thee bedside table. It glides two inches toward you—then stops. You stare. The cup sits ordinary and still, as if the pine-sap glaze had never moved. Down in the lane a cart wheel squeals, someone laughs, and a dropped crate thuds against packed dirt.

Boots thump on the stair. Outside the cracked window the market is stirring: vendors shouting prices, a dog barking at geese, the faint ring of the blacksmith’s hammer. You can pull on your coat and step out, or linger here a moment longer.

