The star-maps on Zareth’s forearms dim to a steady pulse, like a heartbeat settling.  
He folds both hands inside his wide sleeves and simply nods once—no flourish, no extra words.  

“Good,” he says. “Then the path is set. Walk south from Solmara’s gate until the cobbles end; the Whispering Woods begin where the fog starts hugging the ground. You’ll smell the sap of the luck-tree on the wind before you see its glow.”  

He turns, already drifting toward the colonnade that leads back to his observatory, voice carrying over his shoulder.  
“Mind the dice-coins in your pockets—probability turns quicker than a thief when that tree wakes. Come back with news, or don’t come back at all.”

