The starlight pool ripples once, then stills. Oracle Zareth’s voice fades, leaving only the hush of the clearing and the sudden crack of underbrush.

A Hollow Stalker bursts through the ferns—gaunt ribs showing beneath patchy fur, eyes milky with hunger. It lands in a crouch between you and the path, claws raking damp leaf-mould.

Captain Oren’s shout cuts the air. “Blade up—now!”

Steel meets claw. The beast lunges; you sidestep, feel hot breath on your sleeve, and drive your weapon down into its spine. A shudder, a gutteral wheeze, then the body folds. Blood steams on the cold ground.

Silence returns, heavier than before. Your pulse hammers; the forest smells of iron and bruised pine.

